# Git

## Commit messages

Match existing history (`JRL-1: initialize project structure`):

```
JRL-<ticket>: <imperative summary>
```

Examples:

- `JRL-2: add spring boot next.js stack and git commands`
- `JRL-3: implement ticket status transitions`

Rules:

- Ticket prefix is `JRL-` plus the integer (next unused number if there is no ticket).
- Imperative, lowercase after the colon, no trailing period.
- Subject line only unless the why needs one extra sentence in the body.
- Do not list every file in the subject.

## What not to commit

- `.env`, credentials, API keys, private keys
- `node_modules/`, `frontend/.next/`, `backend/build/`, `backend/.gradle/`
- Local IDE noise already in `.gitignore`

## Branch and push

- Default: feature branch (`cursor/jrl-<n>-<summary>`), never commit directly to `main` unless the user insists.
- Push only when the user asks. `git push -u origin HEAD`. No `--force` to `main`. No `--no-verify`.
- Open a PR into `main` after push when the user asked for GitHub.

When committing, follow `commands/commit-and-push.md`.
